# TridentStack CVE API

Free, no-auth API for CVE vulnerability data. Returns CVSS, EPSS, CISA KEV status, CWEs, and **remediation** (fixed versions per affected product) — the only free API that does this.

## When to Use

- Lookup a specific CVE by ID (e.g. `CVE-2024-3094`)
- Search CVEs by keyword, severity, EPSS score, or KEV status
- Find **which version fixes** a vulnerability for a specific package
- Batch-check up to 100 CVEs in one request
- Get CVE data in OSV schema (compatible with Trivy, Grype, Renovate)
- Triage vulnerabilities by exploit probability (EPSS) + active exploitation (KEV)

## Prerequisites

- No API key required
- No authentication required
- Rate limit: 60 requests/minute (check `X-RateLimit-Remaining` header)

## Base URL

```
https://tridentstack.com/api/v1
```

## Endpoints

### 1. Get Single CVE (full detail)

```
GET /api/v1/cve/{cveId}
```

Response keys: `cveId`, `description`, `severity`, `cvss`, `epss`, `kev`, `cwes`, `remediation`, `references`, `publishedAt`, `modifiedAt`, `dataSources`, `_links`

`remediation.products[].atoms[]` contains: `fixedVersion`, `advisoryId`, `source`, `sourceUrl`

Invoke through `terminal`:
```bash
curl -s "https://tridentstack.com/api/v1/cve/CVE-2024-3094" | python3 -m json.tool
```

### 2. Get CVE in OSV Schema

```
GET /api/v1/cve/{cveId}/osv
```

Same CVE data in OpenSSF OSV format (schema v1.6.0). Use with vulnerability scanners.

```bash
curl -s "https://tridentstack.com/api/v1/cve/CVE-2024-3094/osv"
```

### 3. Batch Lookup (up to 100 CVEs)

```
POST /api/v1/cve/batch
Content-Type: application/json
Body: {"ids": ["CVE-2024-3094", "CVE-2021-44228"]}
```

Response: `results[]` (full records) + `notFound[]` (unresolved IDs).

```bash
curl -s -X POST "https://tridentstack.com/api/v1/cve/batch" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"ids":["CVE-2024-3094","CVE-2021-44228"]}'
```

### 4. Search & List CVEs

```
GET /api/v1/cve
```

**Query Parameters:**

| Param | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `q` | string | Full-text search (CVE IDs, keywords, products) |
| `severity` | string | `critical`, `high`, `medium`, `low` |
| `kev` | bool | `true` = only CISA Known Exploited Vulns |
| `fix` | bool | `true` = only CVEs with available fixes |
| `epss_min` | float | Minimum EPSS score (0.0 - 1.0) |
| `year` | int | CVE published year (e.g. `2024`) |
| `sort` | string | `published`, `epss`, `cvss`, `cve`, `fix`, `kev` |
| `limit` | int | Results per page (max 100, default 20) |
| `nextCursor` | string | Pagination cursor from previous response |

**Example — critical CVEs with high EPSS, sorted by EPSS:**
```bash
curl -s "https://tridentstack.com/api/v1/cve?severity=critical&epss_min=0.8&sort=epss&limit=5"
```

**Pagination:** Response includes `nextCursor` when more pages exist. Pass it as `?nextCursor=<value>` for the next page.

